==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|present participle}}

# {{present participle of|slight|lang=en|nocat=1}}
#: ''His '''slighting''' of the company chairman was considered to be inappropriate behaviour.''

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# In the manner of a [[slight]]; [[belittling]], [[deprecative]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of giving a [[slight]] or [[snub]].
#* '''1848''', Lucy Hutchinson, ''Memoirs of the life of Colonel Hutchinson'' (page 376)
#*: {{...}} the rest, who had looked upon him with such disdainful neglect {{...}} now flocked about him, striving who should express most respect, and, by an extraordinary officiousness, redeem their late '''slightings'''.
# {{lb|en|regional}} An act of ignoring or neglecting someone or something; more broadly [[neglect]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''slighting''' of childern}}
# {{lb|en|regional}} The action of rejecting someone or something; [[rejection|rejection]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''slighting''' of a handshake by Samuel ticked off Judi to no end.}}
# {{lb|en|military}} The full or partial demolition of a fortification, rendering it no longer defensible.

